    "created_at": "2026-08-06T11:10:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-06T11:10:30Z",
    "body": "Would be really good to get clarity on `javascript:` navigation situation. If `<math:a>` does navigate to `javascript:`-URLs, it'd need to be added to the [built-in navigating url attributes list](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#built-in-navigating-url-attributes-list).\r\n\r\nIn either case, it'd be good to add test cases to [sanitizer-javascript-url](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-javascript-url.html).\r\n\r\nIdeally, we'd also have a test similar in spirit to [sanitizer-svg-animate](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-svg-animate.html), which tests SVG animation+navigation end-to-end and tries to make the navigation happen. [sanitizer-javascript-url](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-javascript-url.html) catches cases where the filtering behaviour deviates from the spec; while [sanitizer-svg-animate](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/sanitizer-api/sanitizer-svg-animate.html) also catches cases where the navigation behaviour is different, too. We had a bug in Chrome where a malformed navigation attribute would (correctly) pass the sanitizer, but would then still cause the navigation to happen. Since this PR makes `<math:a>` to be default-allowed, that extra step would IMHO be worth it.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
