    "created_at": "2026-08-20T13:31:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-08-20T13:31:46Z",
    "body": "> So we should figure out if MathML's `<a>` navigates to javascript:-URLs and if so we should baseline-sanitize them; if not, then not.\r\n\r\nThe argument for sanitizing `javascript:` in `href` in *any* MathML element currently, iirc, is that it will execute script in some existing browsers. This will continue to be true even if the spec is changed to no longer support `javascript:` URLs for MathML/SVG links.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
